  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-915",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "f2605ab1db6e533af29784528501f121cb75af559b3f3925f05998dc3888ac09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2605ab1db6e-0000-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nE. JOSHUA ROSENKRANZ, ESQUIRE, New York, New York; on behalf of the Petitioner.\nMELISSA N. PATTERSON, Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; for the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting the Petitioner.\nPETER K. STRIS, ESQUIRE, Los Angeles, California; on behalf of the Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "E. Joshua Rosenkranz, Esq., on behalf of the Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2021-20-915",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "f2605ab1db6e533af29784528501f121cb75af559b3f3925f05998dc3888ac09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2605ab1db6e-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The question here is what state of mind a copyright infringer must prove to establish that an applicant included inaccurate information \"with knowledge that it was inaccurate.\" The answer is that it requires subjective awareness of what -- of the inaccuracy itself."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-20-915",
      "confidence": 0.99,
      "document_hash": "f2605ab1db6e533af29784528501f121cb75af559b3f3925f05998dc3888ac09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2605ab1db6e-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Can I follow up on that point too?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2021-20-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f2605ab1db6e533af29784528501f121cb75af559b3f3925f05998dc3888ac09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2605ab1db6e-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "All right. One --one other question. In what way could you have been benefited by attempting to register all of these designs on one application as opposed to using a separate application for each design?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Rosenkranz",
      "case_id": "2021-20-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f2605ab1db6e533af29784528501f121cb75af559b3f3925f05998dc3888ac09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2605ab1db6e-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It could not have helped us in any other way, Your Honor. And that's exactly why Congress wrote the statute the way it did, because there's very little"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Melissa N. Patterson",
      "case_id": "2021-20-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f2605ab1db6e533af29784528501f121cb75af559b3f3925f05998dc3888ac09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2605ab1db6e-0001-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress has set out a default rule to preserve the validity of copyright registrations even if they contain some inaccurate information. Under Section 411(b), such a registration remains adequate to support an"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-20-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f2605ab1db6e533af29784528501f121cb75af559b3f3925f05998dc3888ac09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2605ab1db6e-0001-0007",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF MELISSA N. PATTERSON FOR THE UNITED STATES, AS AMICUS CURIAE, SUPPORTING THE PETITIONER"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-20-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f2605ab1db6e533af29784528501f121cb75af559b3f3925f05998dc3888ac09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2605ab1db6e-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, but what do you think of the constructive versus actual debate?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-20-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f2605ab1db6e533af29784528501f121cb75af559b3f3925f05998dc3888ac09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2605ab1db6e-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How about unreasonableness?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-20-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f2605ab1db6e533af29784528501f121cb75af559b3f3925f05998dc3888ac09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2605ab1db6e-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Can I interrupt you on number one?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-20-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f2605ab1db6e533af29784528501f121cb75af559b3f3925f05998dc3888ac09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2605ab1db6e-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: How --I guess I'm not understanding that. If you know that there's a material misstatement of law in an application you're submitting to the office, how do you not have an intent to deceive?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-20-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f2605ab1db6e533af29784528501f121cb75af559b3f3925f05998dc3888ac09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2605ab1db6e-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: What about the word \"information\"?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Stris",
      "case_id": "2021-20-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f2605ab1db6e533af29784528501f121cb75af559b3f3925f05998dc3888ac09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2605ab1db6e-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Jerman was a case where there was a circuit split. There was on-point circuit authority of the position that the defendant took. And the Court still had no trouble finding that mistakes of law don't count because it was looking at the overall context of the statute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Stris",
      "case_id": "2021-20-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f2605ab1db6e533af29784528501f121cb75af559b3f3925f05998dc3888ac09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2605ab1db6e-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our position in terms of looking at that context, when you have a word like \"knowledge\" that does not have, I would submit, the ordinary meaning that it's what you subjectively think, why would the government in that regime confer those privileges on an unreasonable error?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2021-20-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f2605ab1db6e533af29784528501f121cb75af559b3f3925f05998dc3888ac09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2605ab1db6e-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So a lay person who doesn't really know much about copyright but knows how to, you know, write a book or whatever it is that's going to be copyrighted, they don't have to know anything? Is -- is it simply a knew or should have known?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-20-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f2605ab1db6e533af29784528501f121cb75af559b3f3925f05998dc3888ac09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2605ab1db6e-0003-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 73,
        "start": 73
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Two questions. One, doesn't the SG's blending -- or not blending, but bridging of the reasonableness requirement with the knowledge requirement in the footnote I keep mentioning -- doesn't that give you half a loaf at least?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-20-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f2605ab1db6e533af29784528501f121cb75af559b3f3925f05998dc3888ac09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2605ab1db6e-0003-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 75,
        "start": 75
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Second question: The policy arguments back and forth, Solicitor General has come in on the side opposite you."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "E. Joshua Rosenkranz",
      "case_id": "2021-20-915",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f2605ab1db6e533af29784528501f121cb75af559b3f3925f05998dc3888ac09",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f2605ab1db6e-0003-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 78,
        "start": 78
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First, on the merits, Mr. Stris says pretty forthrightly that the statute is ambiguous. I don't think it is. I think it's pretty clear, especially the structure of the statute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2021-20-915",
